The '''Warfaa Period''' ([[Burawi language|Burawi]]: ''Xilligii Warfaa'', from ''warfaa'', "deliverance") was the third major era of the [[Kingdom of Ufyen]], spanning approximately 150 BCE to 400 AD. It encompasses three dynasties — the '''Warfaa''', '''Cigaal''', and '''Liibaan''' — and is characterised by defensive consolidation, territorial contraction, and a revivalist ideology centred on the worship of [[Waaq]] and the memory of the [[Geedi Period]]. The period ended when the formation of the [[Kingdom of Burawa]] in 403 AD destabilised the highland court.

